---
scope: src/service/atomFeed
alignment: unreviewed
description: Renders a valid Atom feed of the site's docs and /learn pages from page data it is handed, so readers and agents learn when content changes.
intent: >
  Feed readers and AI agents subscribe to aidemd.dev to learn when its docs and
  /learn pages change. This module turns the page data it is handed into a
  valid Atom feed whose dates are true: each entry carries its page's real
  last-modified date, the feed's own updated time is its newest entry's date,
  and a page with no known date stays out rather than getting a guessed one.
  Entries point at canonical page addresses, match each page's title and
  summary, and credit Lowmeadow LLC as author. It reads nothing beyond what it
  is given.
outcomes:
  desired:
    - The feed validates as Atom and lists every docs and /learn page it is handed that has a known last-modified date, each entry carrying that page's true date.
    - The feed's own updated time equals its newest entry's date, so rebuilding the site with no content change leaves the feed's dates unchanged.
    - Each entry links to the page's canonical address with its trailing slash, and its title and summary match what the page itself shows.
    - Every entry and the feed name Lowmeadow LLC as author, naming no person.
    - The feed is built only from the page data it is handed, so it lists exactly the pages the rest of the site publishes.
  undesired:
    - A build time, today's date, or any guessed date standing in for a page's real last-modified date, or for the feed's own updated time.
    - A page with no known date included in the feed with a made-up date instead of being left out.
    - An entry pointing at a non-canonical address, such as one missing its trailing slash, or carrying a title or summary the page does not show.
    - A person named as author, or an author other than Lowmeadow LLC.
    - A feed that reads like valid XML but fails Atom validation, so feed readers reject it or show it empty.
---
